      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FAKE FICTION (7) treks across the border, and the Tom Dabernig stable has a good record when racing on this sharp turning circuit. She dons the blinkers for the first time, and should go close to winning this. VIPERSTRIKE (5) has shown enough talent in 4 starts to be considered a threat in this field, and a recent jump-out should have him spot on after a freshen up. Each way. BRAZEN QUEEN (6) will find this easier than her last start, and she was near enough in similar fields to this before that. Stick with her on an each-way basis. NICALOHA (3) won a couple of jump-outs and then failed to race up to expectations fresh up as the favourite. He will be better for it, and is worth another chance in this modest field. Follow your money. CALM THE PRESS (1) had a tough trip and faded out of it last time out, and he can bounce back into form here,",
